"""Level Factory 0.232.0 (the factory's roadmap 296): a level's package names the buildings it stands, and
carries their drawings.

The building library reports each row's Deli Counter spec, the compose names it (`--spec`, and `shell_spec` for the
mission's own building) so Deli Counter 0.257.0 draws each building into its package, and the export writes
`buildings.json` at the package's root: every standing instance, where it stands, and its drawings as `res://` paths
the closure verdict resolves.

What this writes, every target pinned by its hash and refused on a mismatch, nothing written until every file has been
worked out: `packages/pipeline/building_library.py`, `apps/cli/commands/__init__.py`,
`adapters/presentation/__init__.py`, `assets/scripts/run_presentation_compose.py` and `packages/exporting/export.py`
(anchored hunks); the new `packages/exporting/buildings_index.py`, `tests/unit/test_buildings_index.py` and
`tests/unit/test_compose_draws_its_buildings.py`; VERSION; the CHANGELOG entry, prepended. Generated from a proven
clone (`patches/lf_drawings/gen_lf_drawings.py`), dry-run on a fresh clone to the clone's every byte, a second run
refused (`patches/lf_drawings/dry_run_*.out.txt`).

    python patches/patch_lf_drawings.py
    cd level_factory && python -m pytest -q
"""
